  "answer": "A synapse is the functional region where information is transferred between two neurons. When a stimulus is received by the dendrites of a neuron, it triggers a chemical reaction that creates an electrical impulse. This impulse travels through the cell body and axon of the neuron. At the synapse, chemicals (neurotransmitters) are released from the end of the axon and cross the gap to reach the next neuron, allowing the transfer of information. This process is essential for communication within the nervous system.",
